E
stained glass windows scenes~
   The windows depict scenes of the Death Knights of legend.  You notice that
not every window contains a scene.  Perhaps, someday, an artisan may fashion a
window for you.  The windows display the Knights Kurse and Aggression.    
~
E
kurse~
   The stained glass shows Lord Kurse, dressed in black full plate.  He stands
atop a hill and is raising his outstretched arms to young knights.  Kurse was
known for helping to organize the knighthood.  He called together young knights
who would one day take over the knighthood's leadership when he departed.    
~
E
aggression~
   This window shows Aggresssion wearing the shining armor of a paladin.  He is
shown deep in a dungeon, plundering its riches.  Aggression was once a mislead
Solamnic Knight.  As the spirit of Aggression took him, he became one of the
most renown questing knights of the order.    
~
S
#38509
The temple dungeons~
   You have entered a portion of Hellfire Keep's dungeons.  Here, captured
slaves are kept alive for the Death Knights to use as they will.  This often
includes sacrifice in the temple above or torture for the amusement of the
Knights.  Death Knights draw much of their power from the suffering of others
and the dungeons are kept well stocked for this purpose.    
~
